{"tool_name":"kled","contents":["bioconda","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"kled","version":"1.2.11","home":"https://github.com/CoREse/kled","documentation":"https://github.com/CoREse/kled/blob/v1.2.11/README.md","license":"MIT","summary":"An ultra-fast and sensitive structural variant detection tool for long-read sequencing data.","identifiers":["biotools:kled","doi:10.1093/bib/bbae049","doi:10.3389/fgene.2024.1435087"],"description":"Kled is designed to call SVs nicely and quickly using long-read sequencing data. \nIt takes mapped reads file (bam) as input and reports SVs to the stdout in the \nVCF file format. Kled can yield precise and comprehensive SV detection results \nwithin minutes and can run on any modern computer without needing of any field \nknowledge of the user to perform the SV detection.\n","license_file":"LICENSE","build":{"number":0,"run_exports":[null],"skip":true},"requirements":{"build":[null,"cmake","make","automake","autoconf","libtool","pkg-config","clangdev"],"host":["zlib","bzip2","liblzma-devel","libcurl","openssl","libdeflate","boost-cpp >=1.84","gmp","libgomp","llvm-openmp","openmpi"],"run":["boost-cpp >=1.84","gmp","libgomp","llvm-openmp","openmpi"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/CoREse/kled/releases/download/v1.2.11/kledv1.2.11.allmodules.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["kled --help","kled --version"]},"recipe_maintainers":["CoREse"]},"biotools":{"id":"kled","home":"https://github.com/CoREse/kled","summary":"Ultra-fast and sensitive structural variant detection tool for long-read sequencing data.","addition_date":"2024-05-23T23:45:50.803428Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T13:56:39.106305Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:kled","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"ydwang@hit.edu.cn","name":"Yadong Wang","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6500-6217","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"bo.liu@hit.edu.cn","name":"Bo Liu","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"ydliu@hit.edu.cn","name":"Yadong Liu","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"De-novo assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0524"},{"term":"Genotyping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196"},{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"}]}],"name":"kled","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bib/bbae049","metadata":{"abstract":"Structural Variants (SVs) are a crucial type of genetic variant that can significantly impact phenotypes. Therefore, the identification of SVs is an essential part of modern genomic analysis. In this article, we present kled, an ultra-fast and sensitive SV caller for long-read sequencing data given the specially designed approach with a novel signature-merging algorithm, custom refinement strategies and a high-performance program structure.The evaluation results demonstrate that kled can achieve optimal SV calling compared to several state-of-the-art methods on simulated and real long-read data for different platforms and sequencing depths.Furthermore,kled excels at rapid SV calling and can efficiently utilize multiple Central Processing Unit (CPU) cores while maintaining low memory usage. The source code for kled can be obtained from https://github.com/CoREse/kled.","authors":[{"name":"Cao S."},{"name":"Jiang T."},{"name":"Li G."},{"name":"Liu B."},{"name":"Liu Y."},{"name":"Wang Y."},{"name":"Zhang Z."}],"citationCount":3,"date":"2024-03-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Briefings in Bioinformatics","title":"Kled: an ultra-fast and sensitive structural variant detection tool for long-read sequencing data"},"pmcid":"PMC10883419","pmid":"38385878"}],"topic":[{"term":"Genotype and phenotype","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0625"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"},{"term":"Structural variation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3175"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"kled",